    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d308">

                <pb facs="0428" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg322"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Señor
                            Lazcano</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-07-09"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your note of the 4th instant, I
                    have the honor to say that a copy of the telegram of May 8 last from our consul
                    at Valparaiso, containing the declarations of the South American Steamship
                    Company concerning the ownership of the <hi rendition="#italic">Itata</hi>, also
                    a copy of your note, have been sent to the Attorney-General for his
                    information.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
